    "id": "lem:common-marginal-poisson-prior",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "There are constants \\(b_\\epsilon,\\gamma_\\epsilon,c_\\epsilon,C_\\epsilon>0\\) such that the finite-atom construction in \\(\\mathrm{def:common\\mbox{-}marginal\\mbox{-}prior\\mbox{-}handle}\\), with \\(L\\ge2\\), \\(B=b_\\epsilon L/M\\), \\(a=\\gamma_\\epsilon B/L^2\\), and \\(k\\) rare cells, has the following properties whenever \\(ka\\le c_\\epsilon\\): it lies in \\(\\mathcal M_{d,\\epsilon}\\), its two priors have exactly the same distribution of the full random table \\(P_{XA}\\), its raw target centers are separated by at least \\(c_\\epsilon ka\\), its raw mass and target variances are at most \\(C_\\epsilon kBa\\), and the total variation distance of the two mixture laws in a Poisson experiment of labeled intensity \\(u\\) and auxiliary intensity \\(v\\), \\(M=u+v\\), is at most\n\\[\n C_\\epsilon uka\\rho_\\epsilon^L\n\\]\nfor a fixed \\(0<\\rho_\\epsilon<1\\).  The likelihood discrepancy is gated by the labeled intensity \\(u\\), although \\(M\\) includes all auxiliary observations.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(P\\)",
      "\\(P_{XA}\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal M_{d,\\epsilon}\\)",
      "\\(\\Pi_0\\)",
      "\\(\\Pi_1\\)",
      "\\(\\epsilon\\)",
      "\\(d\\)",
      "\\(p_x\\)",
      "\\(e_x\\)",
      "\\(\\mu_{ax}\\)",
      "\\(\\tau(P)\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:overlap",
      "def:model-class",
      "def:ate-functional",
      "def:common-marginal-prior-handle",
      "lem:finite-alternation-duality",
      "lem:common-marginal-uniform-intensity"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Apply \\(\\mathrm{lem:common\\mbox{-}marginal\\mbox{-}uniform\\mbox{-}intensity}\\) with \\(B=b_\\epsilon L/M\\).  Then \\(MB=b_\\epsilon L\\), so (C42) holds whenever \\(ka\\le c_\\epsilon\\).  Its membership, exact random-\\(P_{XA}\\) equality, center separation, variance, and total-variation conclusions are exactly those asserted here.  In particular the likelihood bound contains \\(u\\), because (C48) is identically zero until at least one labeled treated outcome mark occurs; the auxiliary intensity enters only through \\(M=u+v\\).",
